{
  "about": "Which path answers a query, and whether the answer is right.",
  "why": [
    "The tool-use suite measures a model. This measures the launcher.",
    "Almost everything typed into Celeritas never reaches a model: arithmetic, units, currency, share and coin prices, emoji, app names. Our own code decides which of those handles a query, and that decision is invisible until it is wrong.",
    "It has been wrong twice in one day. 'am i free today' was taken by the clock because the trigger word 'today' appeared at the end. '1 eth to sol' was passed to a model, which answered 66 from prices it half remembered when the real answer was 23.6.",
    "Both are the same failure: a query went down the wrong path. One showed a wrong section, the other spent money to be wrong."
  ],
  "fields": {
    "query": "what someone types",
    "section": "the section that must appear",
    "forbid": "sections that must not appear",
    "contains": "text the answer must contain, for the cases where correctness is checkable",
    "note": "why this case exists, when it is not obvious"
  },
  "cases": [
